  "question": {
    "text": "Two number $\\mathrm{k}_1$ and $\\mathrm{k}_2$ are randomly chosen from the set of natural numbers. Then, the probability that the value of $\\mathrm{i}^{\\mathrm{k}_1}+\\mathrm{i}^{\\mathrm{k}_2},(\\mathrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1})$ is non-zero, equals",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "dz9M4",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9GK3X",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "6FgqG",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HwW1a",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $k_1=4 \\lambda_1+r_1, r_1 \\in\\{0,1,2,3\\}$\n$k_2=4 \\lambda_2+r_2$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& (i)^{k_1}+(i)^{k_2}=(i)^{r_1}+(i)^{r_2} \\\\\n& (i)^{r_1} \\in\\{1, i,-1,-i\\}\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\text { Zero } \\Rightarrow 1,(-1) \\text { pair } \\quad \\Rightarrow\\left\\{\\begin{array}{cc}\n1, & -1 \\\\\ni, & -i \\\\\n-i,+i \\\\\n-1, & 1\n\\end{array}\\right\\}$\n$i,(-i)$ pair\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { Zero probability }=\\frac{4}{{ }^4 C_1 \\cdot{ }^4 C_1}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ & \\text { Probability (non-zero) }=1-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
